            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love gimlets and this one was pretty good, although I liked it even better when I made it again with more simple syrup. For a balanced drink, you should use about 1/2 ounce of simple syrup, which is 3 teaspoons/1 tablespoon, like in the video.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-13T23:02:11.253Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FRITZIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a 50s themed party with friends as that was a common drink at that time. I used Tanquary Gin, lemon juice and simple syrup (leftover from preserving peaches) plus a slice of lime. It was tart, a little too tart for me but some guests liked the tartness. If I was to make it again, I would sweeten it up a bit.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-04T15:37:58.897Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "newmexjags"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love gin and I love lime. I notice that the video called for 1 tablespoon simple syrup instead of 1 teas. I ended up using 2 tablespoons. Don't use Rose's, it has high fructose corn syrup. Yuk! Making your own simple syrup is easy, just 1:1 sugar and water, bring to a boil then pour into a bottle. It lasts for a long time. My husband prefers vodka. I didn't think it was as tasty a drink with vodka. This is nice for hot summer evenings!",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-22T22:33:32.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Palomino Girl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved it, however I used Rose's sweetened lime juice. I'm thinking straight lime juice would lock my dang jaws! ??",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-05T02:04:20.820Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lexicon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use Rose's sweetened lime juice. Simple syrup and fresh lime juice make this an average drink. I prefer Vodka over Gin. A vodka Gimlet is a delicious lime tasting drink.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-22T05:10:42.243Z"
          }
